 Requests and responses are bounded to 131072 encoded bytes. Transcript content is bounded to 98304 bytes; responses contain at most 128 strict NDJSON frames, each at most 16384 bytes, with at most 65536 output bytes. Only the exact POST URL and reconstructed JSON/NDJSON headers are accepted. Redirects, encoding variants, duplicate/unknown fields, arbitrary destinations and caller authorization/proxy headers deny. The DO owns credentials, finite stream cancellation and credential-echo rejection. Malformed/truncated responses retain uncertain admitted evidence and cannot redispatch automatically. Known failures and adapter terminal errors retain the prepared model/provider identity, including the explicitly synthetic supported `faux-2` model. That fixture catalogue is not live account entitlement. No credential enters the runtime or execution sandbox.
 
