+The synthetic product transport phase has independent local acceptance. The subsequent configuration candidate still requires independent review. Neither phase establishes hosted acceptance. Live discovery/transport and PD38 remain `not run`.
+
+The fixture configuration candidate adds separate strict V1 configuration intents, acknowledgments and snapshots. Historical CommandV1 and SnapshotV1 schemas retain their meanings. The modelConfiguration readiness query remains unchanged. Production configuration and discovery remain unavailable.
+
+Deployment-owned subject context, not intent fields, authenticates configuration through private product Worker RPC. A separate D1 owned-session policy checks current user/project/session ownership, trusted runtime owner version, exact execution identity and retirement/deletion fences without inventing a prompt or model attempt. New selections additionally require the current credential DO connection and exact synthetic connection/capability generation, revision, model and thinking entitlement. Owned configuration reads and duplicate receipts need no new model entitlement. Each provider attempt still performs its independent mandatory admission checks.
+
+The runtime serializes configuration with its existing owner lane and applies it through supported Pi configuration. Intent identities bind the authenticated owner, project, session, owner version and intent ID. Canonical payload digests detect changed-payload conflicts. Runtime intent outcomes are encrypted under the same retained-state owner/session binding as other private host evidence. D1 stores no model selection authority.
+
+A durable pending intent precedes Pi configuration. An acknowledgment follows Pi durability and a persisted-state snapshot. These commits are not a distributed transaction. Reopen never reapplies a pending choice: an exact persisted Pi match completes its original acknowledgment; otherwise its outcome becomes unknown. A pending intent prevents a later selection in that live owner until reopen accounts for it. Older duplicates return their retained outcome, including after a newer selection, without rolling Pi state backward. Current snapshots read persisted Pi agent state, not the intent ledger.
+
+Before creating the first owned Pi root conversation, the runtime validates the explicit default through current product and local authority. Rejection creates no conversation. Standalone synthetic fixtures retain their explicit fixture initialization. Configuration does not grant scheduling or provider authority, and changing selection does not alter already-prepared generation or custom-summary requests. Actual private-adapter fixtures exercise encrypted close/reopen retention, new preparation on retry/follow-up/summary, held authority revocation, and bounded configuration close.
 
